     "result_text_tail": "ce the CEO and leadership team approving the plan.\n- **12% for mid-market** goes one step past the tested 10%. The test covered new sign-ups, not renewals.\n- **The SMB test rate is 8%,** the same as the 2023 rise, the only one with a known churn reaction.\n- **Half of SMB renewals are assumed to fall after July.**\n- **The promotion cohort keeps today's price** through 2027.\n- **The 15% target starts from the $86.0M base**, which comes from mid-2026, as the target itself states.\n\nEvery number traces to the briefing pack or a calculation from it, 131 in all, and no \"?\" placeholders remain. QA passes with no failures. One warning remains: the \"three times the churn rate\" figure is quoted from the pack in words, so the checker can't match it to a digit. I couldn't view the slides as images here, so the layout check rests on the renderer's own warnings, which are all cleared. Worth a quick look before you present.\n\nOf the 12 hypotheses tested, 6 were confirmed and 4 revised. Two were refuted: \"12% raises $10.3M in 2027\" and \"onboarding halves churn\". Data the plan still lacks is listed on the last backup slide: monthly renewal calendar, mid-market seat mix, SMB plan mix, new-customer bookings and onboarding cost.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- palisade-pricing-2027.pptx\n- palisade-pricing-2027-sources.xlsx\n- palisade-pricing-2027.json\n\nThe build scripts are in `./work/`. I can switch the theme, or rerun the numbers with 10% for mid-market or a different SMB rate if you'd prefer."
